y (Voter Parking on the West side of the building) October 17, 2026 Alternate Site starts at the Moriarty Civic Center 10 am - 6pm, Tuesday - Saturday Information About Open Primary Elections - Did you know DTS Voters and Minor Party Voters can NOW vote in the Primary Election? New Information on Open Primary Elections: Major Party Voters - Registered with a Major Party? Democrat & Republican can only vote for their parties and CAN NOT change their party affiliation. Minor Party Voters - Registered with a Minor Party? Libertarian & Independent Party CAN NOT vote in the primary, unless they change their party affiliation to either Democrat of Republican or DTS DTS (Decline to State) voters - CAN vote in the primary. DTS Voters will have to indicate to the poll official what party ballot they would like. Please review a SAMPLE BALLOT to ensure what party ballot you would like to vote, before indicating to the poll official what ballot you are requesting. Are you interested in being a Poll Worker??? NM Secretary of State General Information Employment Opportunities Procurement Road Maintenance Request Form Sign Request Form Programs & Services Domestic Violence Program Memorial Page Staff Email Login ©2026 Torrance County, New Mexico all rights reserved | Website Design and Development by Lobo Internet Services"
